.TH WERKMEISTER-WORKSPACE-ABANDON 1 "" "werkmeister" "Werkmeister Manual"
.SH NAME
werkmeister\-workspace\-abandon \- End a workspace without shipping: record the reason in closeout.md and the PR files, push every branch and keep them, remove the workspace
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBwerkmeister workspace abandon\fR <reason> [name]
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-y, \-\-yes\fR
Skip the confirmation prompt
.TP
\fB\-\-skip\-postmortem <reason>\fR
Close out without a post\-mortem; the reason goes in closeout.md
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Ends a workspace whose work won't ship: superseded, out of scope, or stopped. Like \fBwerkmeister workspace close\fR, it refuses without \fBpostmortem.md\fR unless \fB\-\-skip\-postmortem\fR gives a reason. Then it records the reason in \fBcloseout.md\fR and the PR files, pushes every code branch that has commits of its own and keeps it, and removes the workspace. On the issue it posts \fBAbandoned: <reason>\fR and moves it to the \fBabandoned\fR status (on Jira none by default, a comment only; on GitHub closed as not planned; see Issue status). Use \fBwerkmeister workspace close\fR instead once every PR has shipped, or with \fB\-\-no\-pr\fR when the work changed no repo. It lists terminal Claude sessions still open in the workspace.
.PP
The full process is in docs/workspace\-lifecycle.md.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
werkmeister workspace abandon "superseded by SW\-200"
werkmeister workspace abandon "superseded by SW\-200" my\-feature
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBwerkmeister\fR(1)
